<protocol name="variant_management" type="decision" domain="catalog">

## PURPOSE

Protocol for managing product variants within families.
Ensures consistent variant structure, SKU generation, and parent-child relationships.

---

## VARIANT ARCHITECTURE

```
product_families
    |
    +-- variant_axes (size, color, cap_type)
    |       |
    |       +-- variant_values ([size], [color], [design])
    |
    +-- products (individual SKUs)
            |
            +-- product_variant_values (links product to its variant values)
```

**Key Relationships:**
- Family has 1-N axes (how products vary)
- Axis has 1-N values (what variations exist)
- Product has 1 value per axis (specific combination)

---

## VARIANT AXES DESIGN

### Common Axes by Product Type

| Product Type | Typical Axes |
|--------------|--------------|
| Food Jars | size, color, cap_type |
| Beverage Bottles | size, color, neck_type |
| Industrial Containers | size, material_grade, color |
| Cosmetic Packaging | size, color, finish |
| Apparel | size, color, fit |

### Axis Naming Conventions

| Convention | Example | Usage |
|------------|---------|-------|
| snake_case internal | cap_type | `name` column |
| Title Case display | Cap Type | `display_label` column |
| Schema.org mapping | size, color | `schema_property` column |

### Axis Record Structure

| Field | Required | Purpose |
|-------|----------|---------|
| product_family_id | Yes | FK to owning family |
| name | Yes | snake_case identifier (size, cap_type) |
| display_label | Yes | Human-readable (Size, Cap Type) |
| sort_order | Yes | Position in SKU generation |
| schema_property | No | Schema.org mapping for SEO |

---

## VARIANT VALUES DESIGN

### Value Conventions

| Field | Convention | Example |
|-------|------------|---------|
| value | lowercase, identifier | [size], [color], [design] |
| display_label | Human-readable | 500 ML, Blue, Diamond Cap |
| sku_code | UPPERCASE, short | 500ML, BLU, DIA |

### SKU Code Patterns

| Axis | Value | SKU Code |
|------|-------|----------|
| size | [size-a] | [SIZE-A] |
| size | [size-b] | [SIZE-B] |
| color | clear | CLR |
| color | blue | BLU |
| cap_type | diamond | DIA |
| cap_type | ribbed | RIB |

### Value Record Structure

| Field | Required | Purpose |
|-------|----------|---------|
| variant_axis_id | Yes | FK to owning axis |
| value | Yes | lowercase identifier ([size], [color]) |
| display_label | Yes | Human-readable (500 ML, Blue) |
| sku_code | Yes | UPPERCASE, short for SKU generation |
| price_adjustment | No | Price delta from base (default 0) |
| sort_order | Yes | Display ordering |

---

## SKU GENERATION

### Pattern

```
{family_sku_prefix}-{axis1_sku_code}-{axis2_sku_code}-...
```

### Examples

| Family Prefix | Size | Color | Cap | Generated SKU |
|---------------|------|-------|-----|---------------|
| [PREFIX-A] | [SIZE-1] | [CLR-X] | [CAP-1] | [PREFIX-A]-[SIZE-1]-[CLR-X]-[CAP-1] |
| [PREFIX-A] | [SIZE-2] | [CLR-Y] | [CAP-2] | [PREFIX-A]-[SIZE-2]-[CLR-Y]-[CAP-2] |
| [PREFIX-B] | [SIZE-3] | [CLR-Z] | - | [PREFIX-B]-[SIZE-3]-[CLR-Z] |

### SKU Generation Logic

```
1. Get family sku_prefix
2. For each axis (in sort_order):
   a. Get product's variant_value for this axis
   b. Get variant_value.sku_code
   c. Append to SKU with separator
3. Result: {prefix}-{code1}-{code2}-{code3}
```

---

## PRODUCT-VARIANT LINKING

Each product must link to exactly ONE value per axis via `product_variant_values` junction.

### Validation Rules

| Rule | Constraint |
|------|------------|
| Complete coverage | Product has value for each axis in family |
| Single selection | Product has exactly ONE value per axis |
| Unique combinations | No duplicate variant combinations within family |

---

## QUERYING VARIANTS

| Query Need | Approach |
|------------|----------|
| Family variant structure | Query product_families with relations: variant_axes, variant_values |
| Product's variant values | Query products with relations through product_variant_values |
| Products by variant value | Query product_variant_values filtered by variant_value_id |

---

## ADDING NEW VARIANTS

| Scenario | Action | Impact |
|----------|--------|--------|
| New value to existing axis | Create variant_values record linked to axis | New SKU combinations available |
| New axis to family | Create variant_axes record linked to family | All existing products need values for new axis |

---

## VARIANT MATRIX

For a family with M sizes and N colors, the variant matrix is:

| Size | Color | SKU |
|------|-------|-----|
| [SIZE-1] | [CLR-A] | [PREFIX]-[SIZE-1]-[CLR-A] |
| [SIZE-1] | [CLR-B] | [PREFIX]-[SIZE-1]-[CLR-B] |
| [SIZE-2] | [CLR-A] | [PREFIX]-[SIZE-2]-[CLR-A] |
| [SIZE-2] | [CLR-B] | [PREFIX]-[SIZE-2]-[CLR-B] |
| [SIZE-3] | [CLR-A] | [PREFIX]-[SIZE-3]-[CLR-A] |
| [SIZE-3] | [CLR-B] | [PREFIX]-[SIZE-3]-[CLR-B] |

Not all combinations may be valid - sparse matrices are common.

---

## PRICE ADJUSTMENTS

Each variant value can have a price adjustment:

| Axis | Value | Adjustment |
|------|-------|------------|
| size | [size-1] | [Currency] 0 (base) |
| size | [size-2] | +[Currency] [amount] |
| size | [size-3] | +[Currency] [amount] |
| color | [color-a] | [Currency] 0 (base) |
| color | [color-b] | +[Currency] [amount] |

**Final Price = Base Price + Sum(Adjustments)**

Example: [Size B] [Color] = Base + [adj-1] + [adj-2] = Base + [total]

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Correct Approach |
|--------------|---------|------------------|
| Flat product list | "[Product] [size] [color]" as separate unlinked items | Family with axes [size, color], products linked via variant values |
| Inconsistent SKU codes | "[size]", "[size]ml", "[SIZE]ML", "[ALIAS]" mixed | Consistent pattern: "[SIZE-CODE]" (UPPERCASE) |
| Missing variant links | Product without product_variant_values | Always create junction records for family with axes |

</protocol>
